WEBVTT

00:00:00.222 --> 00:00:01.412
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Speaker 1

00:00:02.429 --> 00:00:04.320
<v><b>Speaker 1:</b></v> …the house where we are now,

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:07.225
I drive east into the sun in the morning to get to work

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.807
and west into the sun in the evening to get home.

00:00:10.164 --> 00:00:16.693
So, today, like every sunny day now, I have to half-close my eyes to drive,

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:21.134
I’m squinting all the way there for 40 minutes, and the same on the way home…

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:24.470
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Speaker 2

00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:30.399
<v><b>Speaker 2:</b></v> …so as soon as I realized it actually was him, I immediately turned away,

00:00:30.612 --> 00:00:33.950
and then I glanced at him again just to make completely sure,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.492
and took another peek to see who he was with.

00:00:36.889 --> 00:00:40.258
I think it was his wife and maybe his agent or something.

00:00:40.694 --> 00:00:45.437
I texted my brother who’s a real fan, and he wanted me to go up and say hello,

00:00:45.437 --> 00:00:47.258
but I wouldn’t have dreamed of doing that…

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:50.722
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Speaker 3

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:54.742
<v><b>Speaker 3:</b></v> …I mean, you would think nowadays everybody knows

00:00:54.766 --> 00:00:58.142
how rude it is to talk loudly on your phone on public transport.

00:00:58.508 --> 00:01:03.157
So, I stared hard at him to see if he’d get the message, but he didn’t.

00:01:03.418 --> 00:01:07.652
Then, a few minutes later, he caught my eye and I just glared,

00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:12.220
and though he didn’t hang up, at least he started speaking a bit more quietly…

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:15.471
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Speaker 4

00:01:16.273 --> 00:01:19.008
<v><b>Speaker 4:</b></v> …and after crawling along in the traffic for a bit,

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.551
we noticed that there was a car on fire by the side of the road,

00:01:23.947 --> 00:01:27.252
and, would you believe it, instead of just driving past,

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:31.138
everyone was slowing down and gawping at the fire engine

00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:33.125
and the ambulance and everything…

00:01:35.069 --> 00:01:36.407
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Speaker 5

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:41.244
<v><b>Speaker 5:</b></v> …so I was pretty late anyway, but she wasn’t there when I got there,

00:01:41.277 --> 00:01:44.429
so I looked around and I caught a glimpse of her red coat.

00:01:44.628 --> 00:01:49.267
She was walking away down the road, so I ran after her, shouting ‘Gill! Gill!’,

00:01:49.448 --> 00:01:53.868
and got right up behind her and she turned around, and it wasn’t her!

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:57.260
She just gave me a blank stare. So embarrassing.